@startuml enrol
!theme plain
title Enrolment: a person enrols a subscription once, through the vendor's own flow; the material lands only in the broker's store

actor "Person (owner)" as P
participant "claude / codex CLI\n(vendor flow)" as V
participant "curator broker enrol\n(CLI, as the person's OS user)" as C
participant "Broker daemon\n(service user cur-s-broker)" as B
database "Secret store\n(0600 files, broker user)" as S

== Claude subscription ==
P -> V: claude setup-token (browser login)
V --> P: one-year token (printed, not stored)
P -> C: curator broker enrol claude_code --account ivan/claude/personal --token-stdin [--issued-at]
C -> B: hello; account.enrol {kind: claude-oauth-token, material}
B -> B: peer UID from the kernel = owner UID
B -> S: put(material)
B --> C: account/1 {state: active, expires_at: computed | null}

== Codex personal plan ==
P -> V: codex login (in the home the auth owner will own)
P -> C: curator broker enrol codex_cli --account ivan/codex/personal --chatgpt
C -> B: account.enrol {kind: codex-chatgpt, home handover}
B -> B: refuse a keyring-backed store; take the exclusive lock on auth.json
B --> C: account/1 {state: active}; auth owner started
@enduml
